# Database Paths Quick Reference

> **Full documentation**: [docs/storage/README.md](mdc:docs/storage/README.md)

## ⚠️ DEV vs PROD - DIFFERENT PATHS!

| Environment | Run Command | Database Location |
|-------------|-------------|-------------------|
| **Development** | `.\scripts\code.bat` | `%APPDATA%\code-oss-dev\User\.safe-appeals-navigator\` |
| **Production** | Installed app | `%APPDATA%\Void\User\.safe-appeals-navigator\` |

---

## Development Paths (MOST COMMON)

**⚠️ Development has TWO directories - don't confuse them!**

### 1. Extensions Only (NOT our databases)
```
C:\Users\[USER]\.vscode-oss-dev\
└── extensions\     ← Just installed extensions
```

### 2. Our Databases (APP DATA)
```
C:\Users\[USER]\AppData\Roaming\code-oss-dev\User\.safe-appeals-navigator\
└── databases\
    └── workspaces\
        └── [workspaceHash]\
            ├── workspace.db    ← RAG metadata
            ├── threads.db      ← Chat threads
            ├── emails.db       ← Email data
            └── chroma\
                └── embeddings.db
```

### Full Dev Path Example
Workspace `d:\Steve\Documents\HumanRights` (hash: `2fb73011`):
```
C:\Users\Steve\AppData\Roaming\code-oss-dev\User\.safe-appeals-navigator\databases\workspaces\2fb73011\threads.db
```

---

## Production Paths

```
C:\Users\[USER]\AppData\Roaming\Void\User\.safe-appeals-navigator\
└── databases\
    └── workspaces\
        └── [workspaceHash]\
            ├── workspace.db
            ├── threads.db
            ├── emails.db
            └── chroma\
```

---

## Quick Debug Commands

```powershell
# List dev workspace databases
dir "$env:APPDATA\code-oss-dev\User\.safe-appeals-navigator\databases\workspaces\"

# List production workspace databases
dir "$env:APPDATA\Void\User\.safe-appeals-navigator\databases\workspaces\"

# Find all .db files in dev
Get-ChildItem "$env:APPDATA\code-oss-dev\User\.safe-appeals-navigator" -Recurse -Filter "*.db"

# Query threads (replace hash)
cd D:\Coding\SafeAppeals2.0
node -e "const Database = require('@vscode/sqlite3').Database; const db = new Database('C:/Users/Steve/AppData/Roaming/code-oss-dev/User/.safe-appeals-navigator/databases/workspaces/2fb73011/threads.db', (err) => { if(err) console.log(err); else db.all('SELECT id FROM threads', (e,r) => { console.log(r); db.close(); }); });"
```

